message: "If you use this result, cite it via this metadata."
title: "fs-lower-bound: a lower bound for the Furstenberg–Sárközy problem"
abstract: >-
  A lower bound for the Furstenberg–Sárközy problem: liminf of
  log D(N) / log N is at least 0.753741541837329405..., via square-DAG
  certificates on square-free composite moduli fed into Krachun's gluing
  machinery. AI-generated results with a human managing the workflow —
  produced by Claude Code (Fable 5, Anthropic) with contributions from
  Codex (GPT 5.6 Sol, OpenAI) and Grok Build (Grok 4.6, xAI); see
  DISCLOSURE.md. Machine-checked end to end in Lean 4 (fs-lower-bound-lean).
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-22
url: "https://github.com/JD-Jones-ASES/fs-lower-bound"
